{"model": "Chatterbox Turbo (MLX 8-bit)", "segments": [{"text": "The limited retry pattern is a great tool for retrying method calls a limited number of times.", "block": 0, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/cf84fc589adcd0e51f057ec8a72bf676c557777a23ebec53721628191cdac7de.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.18], [1, 0.18, 0.44], [2, 0.44, 0.86], [3, 0.86, 1.22], [4, 1.22, 1.44], [5, 1.44, 1.54], [6, 1.54, 1.72], [7, 1.72, 2.02], [8, 2.02, 2.22], [9, 2.22, 2.62], [10, 2.62, 2.88], [11, 2.88, 3.28], [12, 3.28, 3.5], [13, 3.5, 3.74], [14, 3.74, 4.08], [15, 4.08, 4.24], [16, 4.24, 4.56]]}, {"text": "In instances where I want to make an API with a limited number of tries.", "block": 0, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/164974e5fd538529d9d8a5fd3e44314f7c612698f173a7dc94b6e5dbbe38a614.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.18], [1, 0.18, 0.6], [2, 0.6, 0.96], [3, 0.96, 1.1], [4, 1.1, 1.24], [5, 1.24, 1.4], [6, 1.4, 1.54], [7, 1.54, 1.66], [8, 1.66, 2.02], [9, 2.02, 2.26], [10, 2.26, 2.36], [11, 2.36, 2.66], [12, 2.66, 3.04], [13, 3.04, 3.22], [14, 3.22, 3.56]]}, {"text": "I would have my method look like this:", "block": 0, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/07565c1d16dee7511b20e5b359108ed6d335d6cc79550a06d50fe7e41066e3e6.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.38], [2, 0.38, 0.52], [3, 0.52, 0.76], [5, 1.06, 1.28], [6, 1.28, 1.48], [7, 1.48, 1.74]]}, {"text": "```ruby limited_retry.rb", "block": 1, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/a1c8e3470a2b56118f3c8b92663fefa0aeacf24211f7837a144e5a024b0fd042.mp3"}, {"text": "def api_call(args) @retries = 0 begin do_api_call(args) rescue ApiError, Timeout @retries += 1 retry if @retries < 5 end end", "block": 2, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/583b28b1d5bd2280afbf9dc6bd29babf22fbcb850dc5444f2364f2fb69c2abac.mp3"}, {"text": "```", "block": 3, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/faba27802a30ed69fdd58fbe8d4a7ced92838df58b101d9e13317b5269d32846.mp3"}, {"text": "The retry method is really powerful in ruby.", "block": 4, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/17ca323afe177a00d3a9d50d0909051717d2ff6402a871ec0bd822c93dec6c4b.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.18], [1, 0.18, 0.54], [2, 0.54, 0.86], [3, 0.86, 1.12], [4, 1.12, 1.42], [5, 1.42, 1.84], [6, 1.84, 2.18], [7, 2.18, 2.38]]}, {"text": "If a block is rescued, by calling “retry” it will attempt to run that block again.", "block": 4, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/8e3b8800dc0e2df1e5eb67bdb0e6210641dade24b947111650ab1076563c55ed.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.24], [1, 0.24, 0.32], [2, 0.32, 0.48], [3, 0.48, 0.7], [4, 0.7, 1.12], [5, 1.12, 1.54], [6, 1.54, 1.86], [8, 2.8, 2.88], [9, 2.88, 2.98], [10, 2.98, 3.28], [11, 3.28, 3.56], [12, 3.56, 3.7], [13, 3.7, 3.9], [14, 3.9, 4.14], [15, 4.14, 4.48]]}, {"text": "For example, if your server has a spotty connection, it would make sense to retry an API request twice if it failed to reach the server.", "block": 4, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/31d01460c377636f6ebe83daf8aa6cbcce2c165a341371c2bbd81b0ae1e0cd41.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.16], [1, 0.16, 0.56], [2, 1.04, 1.18], [3, 1.18, 1.3], [4, 1.3, 1.6], [5, 1.6, 1.88], [6, 1.88, 2.1], [7, 2.1, 2.46], [8, 2.46, 2.92], [9, 3.36, 3.64], [10, 3.64, 3.72], [11, 3.72, 3.88], [12, 3.88, 4.18], [13, 4.18, 4.48], [14, 4.48, 4.86], [15, 4.86, 5.08], [16, 5.08, 5.3], [17, 5.3, 5.7], [18, 5.7, 6.26], [19, 6.26, 6.88], [20, 6.88, 6.98], [21, 6.98, 7.22], [22, 7.22, 7.42], [23, 7.42, 7.56], [24, 7.56, 7.74], [25, 7.74, 8.02]]}, {"text": "The DefRetry gem by DiegoSalazar can be used to add DSL to your ruby classes that you want to retry a few times.", "block": 5, "audio": "../../../assets/blog-audio/249c494dc430f7073a6ba01498967c571bb4a1cb5ffb3c6aa00bca77d6e321cd.mp3", "words": [[0, 0.0, 0.22], [2, 0.7, 0.94], [3, 0.94, 1.14], [5, 1.9, 2.14], [6, 2.14, 2.28], [7, 2.28, 2.46], [8, 2.46, 2.66], [9, 2.66, 2.84], [10, 2.84, 3.4], [11, 3.4, 3.56], [12, 3.56, 3.7], [13, 3.7, 3.98], [14, 3.98, 4.32], [15, 4.32, 4.56], [16, 4.56, 4.68], [17, 4.68, 4.82], [18, 4.82, 5.0], [19, 5.0, 5.38], [20, 5.38, 5.56], [21, 5.56, 5.7], [22, 5.7, 6.04]]}]}